  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///public/assets/aistudio/Paste_November_05__2026_-_11_11PM_6778efb2"
    end_line: 1599
    content: "# SANJEEVANI TRIAGE\r\n## COMPLETE END-TO-END PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT MASTER PROMPT\r\n### Native Mobile Healthcare Application | Multimodal AI | Intelligent Triage | Emergency Response | Hospital Queue Management\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 1 \342\200\224 PROJECT IDENTITY AND VISION\r\n\r\n## 1.1 Project Name\r\n\r\n**Sanjeevani Triage**\r\n\r\n## 1.2 Product Description\r\n\r\nSanjeevani Triage is an AI-powered, multimodal healthcare triage and hospital queue management platform designed to improve healthcare accessibility in rural, semi-urban, and urban communities.\r\n\r\nThe application simplifies healthcare access by replacing complicated form-based patient interactions with voice-based symptom collection, multilingual AI assistance, prescription scanning, intelligent patient classification, geographical hospital allocation, and emergency SOS assistance.\r\n\r\nThe platform connects patients with healthcare facilities through an intelligent routing system and provides hospital administrators with a priority-based patient management dashboard.\r\n\r\n## 1.3 Core Problem\r\n\r\nPatients frequently encounter the following problems:\r\n\r\n- Long waiting times at hospitals.\r\n- Difficulty explaining symptoms to hospital receptionists.\r\n- Language barriers between patients and healthcare professionals.\r\n- Complicated hospital registration processes.\r\n- Difficulty understanding handwritten prescriptions.\r\n- Lack of organized digital medical records.\r\n- Difficulty identifying appropriate hospitals.\r\n- Delayed identification of emergency patients.\r\n- Inefficient patient queue management.\r\n\r\n## 1.4 Our Solution\r\n\r\nSanjeevani Triage addresses these problems through five core capabilities:\r\n\r\n1. **Voice-to-Token OPD:** Patients describe their symptoms using natural speech and receive a digital OPD token through AI-assisted triage.\r\n2. **Smart Rx Decoder:** Patients photograph prescriptions and receive explanations of reliably readable medicine instructions in their preferred language.\r\n3. **Three-Tier Intelligent Triage:** Patients are classified into self-care, OPD, and emergency pathways.\r\n4. **2.5-Second SOS Emergency System:** Patients can activate an emergency alert through a deliberate press-and-hold interaction.\r\n5. **Hospital Admin Dashboard:** Healthcare staff receive dynamically prioritized patient records rather than relying exclusively on first-in-first-out queues.\r\n\r\n## 1.5 Product Philosophy\r\n\r\n**Zero-UI Healthcare Interaction**\r\n\r\nThe patient application must minimize complicated navigation and text-heavy forms.\r\n\r\nPrimary interactions should use:\r\n\r\n- Voice.\r\n- Camera.\r\n- Large touch controls.\r\n- Native-language communication.\r\n- Location detection.\r\n- Simple visual instructions.\r\n\r\nThe application must be accessible to people with limited digital literacy.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 2 \342\200\224 STRICT ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENTS\r\n\r\n## 2.1 NON-NEGOTIABLE: NATIVE MOBILE APPLICATION\r\n\r\nThe patient-facing application MUST be a genuine native mobile application.\r\n\r\nUse React Native with Expo and TypeScript.\r\n\r\nThe application must be installable on Android and iOS.\r\n\r\nSTRICTLY PROHIBITED:\r\n\r\n- Next.js as the patient frontend.\r\n- React DOM.\r\n- HTML-based patient screens.\r\n- Browser-based mobile interfaces.\r\n- Progressive Web Applications.\r\n- WebView wrappers.\r\n- Websites packaged inside Android applications.\r\n- Simulated native interfaces using browser components.\r\n\r\nEvery patient-facing screen must use React Native components and native device functionality.\r\n\r\nThe hospital administrator dashboard is a separate web application and may use Next.js.\r\n\r\n## 2.2 Three-Application Architecture\r\n\r\nBuild the complete platform as three independently deployable applications sharing one backend.\r\n\r\n**Application A \342\200\224 Patient Mobile App**\r\n\r\nTechnology:\r\n- React Native.\r\n- Expo.\r\n- TypeScript.\r\n- Expo Router.\r\n- NativeWind or React Native StyleSheet.\r\n- Lucide React Native.\r\n\r\nTargets:\r\n- Android.\r\n- iOS.\r\n\r\n**Application B \342\200\224 Backend Orchestration Server**\r\n\r\nTechnology:\r\n- Node.js.\r\n- Express.js.\r\n- TypeScript.\r\n- REST APIs.\r\n- Google Gemini API.\r\n- PostgreSQL.\r\n- Persistent object storage.\r\n- WebSocket or equivalent real-time communication.\r\n\r\n**Application C \342\200\224 Hospital Admin Dashboard**\r\n\r\nTechnology:\r\n- Next.js App Router.\r\n- React.\r\n- TypeScript.\r\n- Tailwind CSS.\r\n- Lucide React.\r\n- Recharts, where useful.\r\n\r\nTarget:\r\n- Desktop browsers.\r\n- Tablets.\r\n\r\n## 2.3 System Architecture\r\n\r\nImplement the following architecture:\r\n\r\nPATIENT MOBILE APPLICATION\r\n\342\206\223\r\nNative Device Services\r\n\342\206\223\r\nBackend API Gateway\r\n\342\206\223\r\nAuthentication and Request Validation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nAI Triage Orchestration\r\n\342\206\223\r\nGemini Multimodal Engine\r\n\342\206\223\r\nClinical Routing Validation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nHospital Allocation Engine\r\n\342\206\223\r\nPostgreSQL Database\r\n\342\206\223\r\nReal-Time Patient Queue\r\n\342\206\223\r\nHOSPITAL ADMIN DASHBOARD\r\n\r\nThe SOS system must have an independent emergency pathway that does not depend on Gemini processing.\r\n\r\nArchitecture principles:\r\n\r\n- Secure server-side AI communication.\r\n- Independent mobile and admin clients.\r\n- Centralized backend business logic.\r\n- Persistent patient and token records.\r\n- Real-time or near-real-time queue updates.\r\n- Replaceable AI model provider.\r\n- Replaceable storage provider.\r\n- Modular service architecture.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 3 \342\200\224 TECHNOLOGY STACK\r\n\r\n## 3.1 Patient Mobile Application\r\n\r\nUse the following technologies:\r\n\r\n| Requirement | Technology |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Mobile framework | React Native |\r\n| Development framework | Expo |\r\n| Language | TypeScript |\r\n| Navigation | Expo Router |\r\n| Styling | NativeWind / StyleSheet |\r\n| Icons | Lucide React Native |\r\n| Camera | expo-camera |\r\n| Audio recording | expo-audio |\r\n| Location | expo-location |\r\n| Haptic feedback | expo-haptics |\r\n| Notifications | expo-notifications |\r\n| Secure storage | expo-secure-store |\r\n| File handling | expo-file-system |\r\n| Network communication | Fetch / Axios |\r\n| Server state | TanStack Query |\r\n| Client state | Zustand |\r\n| Form validation | Zod |\r\n\r\nUse compatible package versions for the selected Expo SDK.\r\n\r\nDo not blindly install outdated packages.\r\n\r\n## 3.2 Backend\r\n\r\n- Node.js.\r\n- Express.js.\r\n- TypeScript.\r\n- Google Gemini API SDK.\r\n- PostgreSQL.\r\n- Prisma ORM.\r\n- Zod validation.\r\n- JWT or secure session-based authentication.\r\n- WebSockets or Server-Sent Events.\r\n- Object storage for audio and image uploads.\r\n\r\n## 3.3 Admin Dashboard\r\n\r\n- Next.js App Router.\r\n- React.\r\n- TypeScript.\r\n- Tailwind CSS.\r\n- Lucide React.\r\n- Recharts.\r\n- TanStack Query.\r\n\r\n## 3.4 AI Engine\r\n\r\nUse Google\'s Gemini multimodal models for:\r\n\r\n- Audio understanding.\r\n- Image understanding.\r\n- Telugu language interpretation.\r\n- Hindi language interpretation.\r\n- English language interpretation.\r\n- Symptom extraction.\r\n- Structured triage recommendations.\r\n- Prescription document interpretation.\r\n\r\nOriginal target: Gemini 1.5 Pro.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT: Verify actual model availability before implementation. If the original model is unavailable, configure a currently supported Gemini multimodal model with equivalent required capabilities.\r\n\r\nDo not hardcode an unavailable model ID throughout the codebase.\r\n\r\nUse a centralized model configuration.\r\n\r\n## 3.5 Initial Setup\r\n\r\nCreate the monorepo:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nmkdir sanjeevani-triage\r\ncd sanjeevani-triage\r\n\r\nmkdir mobile backend admin docs\r\n```\r\n\r\nInitialize the mobile application:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd mobile\r\n\r\nnpx create-expo-app@latest . --template tabs\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstall appropriate Expo-native packages:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpx expo install expo-camera expo-audio expo-location expo-haptics expo-notifications expo-secure-store expo-file-system expo-device expo-constants\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstall shared dependencies:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpm install lucide-react-native zustand @tanstack/react-query zod\r\n```\r\n\r\nInitialize the backend:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd ../backend\r\n\r\nnpm init -y\r\n\r\nnpm install express cors helmet dotenv\r\nnpm install @google/genai\r\nnpm install prisma @prisma/client\r\nnpm install zod jsonwebtoken bcryptjs\r\nnpm install multer\r\nnpm install socket.io\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstall development dependencies:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nnpm install -D typescript tsx @types/node @types/express\r\nnpm install -D @types/cors @types/multer\r\n```\r\n\r\nInitialize the admin dashboard:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd ../admin\r\n\r\nnpx create-next-app@latest . --typescript --tailwind --app\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdjust packages as required by the selected SDK versions.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 4 \342\200\224 COMPLETE PROJECT DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\r\n\r\nMaintain a clean monorepo.\r\n\r\n```text\r\nsanjeevani-triage/\r\n\342\224\202\r\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 mobile/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 _layout.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 (auth)/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 welcome.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 register.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 language.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 (tabs)/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 _layout.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 home.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 records.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tokens.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 profile.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 triage/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 recording.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 result.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 prescription/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 camera.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 result.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hospital/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 recommendation.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 details.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 emergency/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 status.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 profile/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 settings.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 medical-info.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 privacy.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 history/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.tsx\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 common/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 navigation/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 patient/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 triage/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 prescription/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hospital/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 emergency/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 health/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hooks/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 store/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 constants/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 assets/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 images/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 icons/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 audio/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.json\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\r\n\342\224\202\r\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 backend/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middleware/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 validators/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 models/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repositories/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ai/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 storage/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 sockets/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 prisma/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 schema.prisma\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tests/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 uploads/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\r\n\342\224\202\r\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 admin/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 patients/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 emergencies/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 queue/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 analytics/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 settings/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hooks/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\r\n\342\224\202\r\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docs/\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 architecture.md\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database.md\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api-documentation.md\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 setup.md\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 deployment.md\r\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 testing.md\r\n\342\224\202\r\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\r\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou may refine this structure when necessary, but maintain clear architectural separation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 5 \342\200\224 COMPLETE MOBILE APPLICATION UI/UX\r\n\r\n## 5.1 Design Philosophy\r\n\r\nDesign a premium healthcare application with an approachable, trustworthy, minimalist appearance.\r\n\r\nVisual direction:\r\n\r\n- Swiss minimalist design.\r\n- Modern healthcare technology.\r\n- White and off-white backgrounds.\r\n- Deep navy text.\r\n- Teal-green primary accent.\r\n- Soft blue information cards.\r\n- Red emergency actions.\r\n- Rounded surfaces.\r\n- Subtle shadows.\r\n- Carefully controlled glassmorphism.\r\n- Smooth native animations.\r\n\r\nSuggested design tokens:\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\nexport const colors = {\r\n  background: \"#F8F9FA\",\r\n  surface: \"#FFFFFF\",\r\n  primary: \"#0D9488\",\r\n  primaryDark: \"#0F766E\",\r\n  secondary: \"#1E3A5F\",\r\n  text: \"#1F2937\",\r\n  muted: \"#64748B\",\r\n  border: \"#E2E8F0\",\r\n  danger: \"#DC2626\",\r\n  warning: \"#F59E0B\",\r\n  success: \"#16A34A\"\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nUse consistent spacing, typography, icon sizes, and border radii.\r\n\r\nDo not overload the application with excessive cards or decorative graphics.\r\n\r\n## 5.2 Onboarding\r\n\r\nCreate a short onboarding experience.\r\n\r\nScreens:\r\n\r\n1. Welcome to Sanjeevani Triage.\r\n2. Select preferred language.\r\n3. Explain voice-based healthcare access.\r\n4. Explain prescription scanning.\r\n5. Explain emergency SOS.\r\n6. Privacy and permissions explanation.\r\n7. Login or registration.\r\n\r\nAvoid requesting all permissions immediately.\r\n\r\nRequest camera, microphone, location, and notification permissions when their respective features are first used.\r\n\r\n## 5.3 Authentication\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n\r\n- Patient registration.\r\n- Patient login.\r\n- Secure session handling.\r\n- Logout.\r\n- Profile management.\r\n- Preferred language.\r\n- Basic medical information.\r\n\r\nCollect only necessary patient information.\r\n\r\nSupport a demo mode with clearly labelled sample data for hackathon demonstrations.\r\n\r\n## 5.4 Native Navigation\r\n\r\nImplement Expo Router navigation.\r\n\r\nBottom navigation:\r\n\r\n- Home.\r\n- Health Records.\r\n- Central SOS control.\r\n- OPD Tokens.\r\n- Profile.\r\n\r\nThe SOS control should be visually prominent and centrally positioned.\r\n\r\nImplement an accessible side drawer or native navigation panel for:\r\n\r\n- Search.\r\n- Previous triage records.\r\n- Medical history.\r\n- Prescriptions.\r\n- Settings.\r\n- Language.\r\n- Help.\r\n- Logout.\r\n\r\nUse native navigation transitions and safe-area handling.\r\n\r\n## 5.5 Home Screen\r\n\r\nThe home screen must contain:\r\n\r\n1. Patient greeting.\r\n2. Patient profile avatar.\r\n3. Daily Health Insight.\r\n4. Main Voice Triage action.\r\n5. Prescription Scanner action.\r\n6. Latest OPD token.\r\n7. Medical records shortcut.\r\n8. Recent consultation history.\r\n9. Bottom navigation.\r\n10. Prominent SOS control.\r\n\r\nThe home screen must clearly communicate the primary action:\r\n\r\n\"Tell us how you\'re feeling.\"\r\n\r\nPrimary action: Speak Symptoms.\r\n\r\nSecondary action: Scan Prescription.\r\n\r\n## 5.6 Daily Health Insight\r\n\r\nFor the initial prototype, use mocked Health Connect data.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"metrics\": {\r\n    \"steps\": 4200,\r\n    \"sleep_duration_hours\": 5.2,\r\n    \"avg_hr_bpm\": 78\r\n  },\r\n  \"context\": {\r\n    \"location\": \"Visakhapatnam\",\r\n    \"weather\": \"Hot and Humid, 32\302\260C\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nDisplay:\r\n\r\n- Daily steps.\r\n- Sleep duration.\r\n- Average heart rate.\r\n- Relevant non-diagnostic health observations.\r\n\r\nClearly label simulated metrics.\r\n\r\nDo not claim the application has actually accessed Google Health Connect.\r\n\r\nA future native Android Health Connect integration may be implemented separately using the appropriate Android APIs and permissions.\r\n\r\nDo not create unsupported medical diagnoses from this data.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 6 \342\200\224 CORE FEATURE 1: VOICE-TO-TOKEN OPD\r\n\r\n## 6.1 Purpose\r\n\r\nAllow patients to describe their symptoms through natural speech without completing complicated medical forms.\r\n\r\nThis is the central interaction of Sanjeevani Triage.\r\n\r\n## 6.2 UI\r\n\r\nCreate a large circular microphone button.\r\n\r\nDisplay:\r\n\r\n- Microphone icon.\r\n- \"Hold to speak symptoms.\"\r\n- Recording indicator.\r\n- Animated audio waveform.\r\n- Recording duration.\r\n- Cancel control.\r\n- Submit/processing state.\r\n\r\nRecording states:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nIDLE\r\nREQUESTING_PERMISSION\r\nRECORDING\r\nUPLOADING\r\nPROCESSING\r\nSUCCESS\r\nFAILED\r\nCANCELLED\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 6.3 Native Audio Recording\r\n\r\nUse Expo Audio.\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n\r\n- Microphone permission.\r\n- Native audio recording.\r\n- Audio duration.\r\n- Start recording.\r\n- Stop recording.\r\n- Cancel recording.\r\n- File validation.\r\n- Upload.\r\n- Cleanup.\r\n\r\nDo not use browser MediaRecorder APIs.\r\n\r\nUse a robust gesture implementation that handles:\r\n\r\n- Short taps.\r\n- Long presses.\r\n- Touch cancellation.\r\n- Application backgrounding.\r\n- Audio interruptions.\r\n- Permission denial.\r\n\r\n## 6.4 Multilingual Processing\r\n\r\nSupport:\r\n\r\n- Telugu.\r\n- English.\r\n- Hindi.\r\n\r\nExample patient input:\r\n\r\n\"My son\'s stomach is hurting a lot.\"\r\n\r\nThe AI must:\r\n\r\n1. Understand the recorded audio.\r\n2. Identify the language.\r\n3. Extract symptoms.\r\n4. Identify symptom duration where available.\r\n5. Extract relevant details.\r\n6. Identify concerning warning signs.\r\n7. Translate symptoms into English.\r\n8. Determine the appropriate triage pathway.\r\n9. Generate patient instructions in the detected language.\r\n10. Return structured JSON.\r\n\r\nDo not invent missing patient information.\r\n\r\nIf the patient description is insufficient, return an unclear result and request clarification or human assessment.\r\n\r\n## 6.5 Backend Audio Upload\r\n\r\nSend the recorded file using multipart/form-data.\r\n\r\nEndpoint:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /api/v1/triage\r\n```\r\n\r\nFields:\r\n\r\n```text\r\naudio\r\npatient_id\r\nlanguage\r\nlat\r\nlng\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 6.6 OPD Token Generation\r\n\r\nFor valid Tier 2 cases:\r\n\r\n- Generate a unique token on the backend.\r\n- Store the triage record.\r\n- Assign a suitable hospital.\r\n- Assign the clinical department.\r\n- Return token information.\r\n- Display a digital OPD token.\r\n\r\nToken example:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"token_number\": \"OPD-102\",\r\n  \"department\": \"General Medicine\",\r\n  \"hospital_name\": \"Apollo Hospitals, Ramnagar\",\r\n  \"status\": \"waiting\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"medium\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe backend must generate token numbers using a concurrency-safe process.\r\n\r\nThe patient must be able to view previous tokens and current status.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 7 \342\200\224 CORE FEATURE 2: SMART RX DECODER\r\n\r\n## 7.1 Purpose\r\n\r\nAllow patients to photograph physical medical prescriptions and understand reliably readable medicine instructions in their preferred language.\r\n\r\n## 7.2 Native Camera Interface\r\n\r\nUse Expo Camera.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Native camera permission.\r\n- Rear camera by default.\r\n- Live preview.\r\n- Capture button.\r\n- Image preview.\r\n- Retake option.\r\n- Upload progress.\r\n- Processing state.\r\n- Result screen.\r\n\r\n## 7.3 AI Extraction\r\n\r\nGemini should attempt to extract:\r\n\r\n- Medicine name.\r\n- Dosage.\r\n- Frequency.\r\n- Duration.\r\n- Administration instructions.\r\n- Other clearly visible prescription information.\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"success\",\r\n  \"medicines\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"Medicine name\",\r\n      \"dosage\": \"Extracted dosage\",\r\n      \"frequency\": \"Extracted frequency\",\r\n      \"duration\": \"Extracted duration\",\r\n      \"instructions_native\": \"Translated instructions\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"safety_warning\": \"\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 7.4 Prescription Safety Protocol\r\n\r\nThis is a strict safety requirement.\r\n\r\nThe system must never guess:\r\n\r\n- Medicine names.\r\n- Dosages.\r\n- Frequency.\r\n- Duration.\r\n- Administration instructions.\r\n\r\nIf the handwriting is unclear, the image is inadequate, or medicine identity cannot be established reliably, stop extraction.\r\n\r\nReturn:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"unclear\",\r\n  \"medicines\": [],\r\n  \"safety_warning\": \"Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nDo not substitute similar-looking medicines.\r\n\r\nDo not recommend alternative medicines.\r\n\r\nDo not independently prescribe or modify a doctor\'s instructions.\r\n\r\nDisplay extracted results as an interpretation that must be confirmed with a qualified pharmacist or prescribing clinician.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 8 \342\200\224 CORE FEATURE 3: THREE-TIER INTELLIGENT TRIAGE\r\n\r\n## 8.1 Overview\r\n\r\nImplement three healthcare routing tiers.\r\n\r\nTier classification must be validated through backend business logic and clinical safety rules.\r\n\r\nThe AI must assist with information extraction and routing suggestions, not independently diagnose diseases.\r\n\r\n## 8.2 TIER 1 \342\200\224 SELF-CARE\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n- Mild cold.\r\n- Minor non-urgent complaints.\r\n- Mild discomfort without warning signs.\r\n\r\nBehaviour:\r\n\r\n- Provide conservative general self-care information.\r\n- Communicate in the patient\'s language.\r\n- Display a disclaimer.\r\n- Explain warning signs.\r\n- Recommend professional care when appropriate.\r\n- Do not generate an OPD token by default.\r\n- Do not add to the hospital queue.\r\n\r\nDo not automatically classify unclear or incomplete symptoms as Tier 1.\r\n\r\n## 8.3 TIER 2 \342\200\224 OPD\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n- Persistent fever.\r\n- Significant abdominal discomfort.\r\n- Conditions requiring a clinical examination.\r\n- Non-immediate complaints requiring medical assessment.\r\n\r\nBehaviour:\r\n\r\n1. Extract symptoms.\r\n2. Determine the relevant clinical department.\r\n3. Retrieve registered hospitals.\r\n4. Match specialties.\r\n5. Calculate geographical distance.\r\n6. Select the nearest suitable registered hospital.\r\n7. Generate OPD token.\r\n8. Save patient record.\r\n9. Send patient record to dashboard.\r\n10. Display allocation result.\r\n\r\n## 8.4 TIER 3 \342\200\224 EMERGENCY\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n- Severe breathing difficulty.\r\n- Suspected stroke.\r\n- Unconsciousness.\r\n- Severe chest pain.\r\n- Other life-threatening warning signs.\r\n\r\nBehaviour:\r\n\r\n- Escalate immediately.\r\n- Set severity score to 10.\r\n- Display emergency instructions.\r\n- Encourage immediate contact with emergency services.\r\n- Create a Priority 0 event.\r\n- Notify the hospital dashboard.\r\n- Avoid waiting for lengthy AI processing.\r\n\r\nDo not make emergency routing dependent on the completion of unrelated AI operations.\r\n\r\n## 8.5 Severity Score\r\n\r\nUse a scale of 1\342\200\22310.\r\n\r\nSuggested interpretation:\r\n\r\n| Score | Interpretation |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 1\342\200\2233 | Low |\r\n| 4\342\200\2236 | Moderate |\r\n| 7\342\200\2238 | High |\r\n| 9\342\200\22310 | Critical |\r\n\r\nThis score is an application prioritization mechanism, not a validated medical scoring instrument.\r\n\r\nCritical warning signs must override numerical scores.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 9 \342\200\224 CORE FEATURE 4: HOSPITAL ALLOCATION ENGINE\r\n\r\n## 9.1 Location Access\r\n\r\nUse Expo Location.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Request location permission.\r\n- Obtain GPS coordinates.\r\n- Handle denied permission.\r\n- Handle unavailable GPS.\r\n- Provide manual location fallback.\r\n- Send location to backend securely.\r\n\r\n## 9.2 Hospital Registry\r\n\r\nCreate a JSON seed dataset.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n[\r\n  {\r\n    \"hospital_id\": \"HOSP-VZG-001\",\r\n    \"hospital_name\": \"Apollo Hospitals, Ramnagar\",\r\n    \"coordinates\": {\r\n      \"lat\": 17.7124,\r\n      \"lng\": 83.3156\r\n    },\r\n    \"specialties\": [\r\n      \"Cardiology\",\r\n      \"Oncology\",\r\n      \"Neurosciences\",\r\n      \"Gastroenterology\",\r\n      \"Orthopaedics\"\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"hospital_id\": \"HOSP-VZG-002\",\r\n    \"hospital_name\": \"CARE Hospitals, Ramnagar\",\r\n    \"coordinates\": {\r\n      \"lat\": 17.7138,\r\n      \"lng\": 83.3142\r\n    },\r\n    \"specialties\": [\r\n      \"Cardiology\",\r\n      \"Neurology\",\r\n      \"Pulmonology\",\r\n      \"Critical Care\",\r\n      \"General Surgery\"\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"hospital_id\": \"HOSP-VZG-003\",\r\n    \"hospital_name\": \"Medicover Hospital, Maharani Peta\",\r\n    \"coordinates\": {\r\n      \"lat\": 17.7085,\r\n      \"lng\": 83.3005\r\n    },\r\n    \"specialties\": [\r\n      \"Internal Medicine\",\r\n      \"Gynecology\",\r\n      \"Pediatrics\",\r\n      \"General Medicine\"\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"hospital_id\": \"HOSP-VZG-004\",\r\n    \"hospital_name\": \"Icon Krishi Hospitals (KIMS), Sheela Nagar\",\r\n    \"coordinates\": {\r\n      \"lat\": 17.6973,\r\n      \"lng\": 83.1979\r\n    },\r\n    \"specialties\": [\r\n      \"Trauma\",\r\n      \"Orthopaedics\",\r\n      \"Urology\",\r\n      \"Critical Care\"\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n]\r\n```\r\n\r\nTreat the supplied registry as a prototype dataset. Do not claim that hospital availability, acceptance, or emergency capacity has been verified.\r\n\r\n## 9.3 Distance Calculation\r\n\r\nImplement Haversine distance in the backend.\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\nfunction calculateDistance(\r\n  lat1: number,\r\n  lon1: number,\r\n  lat2: number,\r\n  lon2: number\r\n): number {\r\n  const R = 6371;\r\n\r\n  const dLat = (lat2 - lat1) * Math.PI / 180;\r\n  const dLon = (lon2 - lon1) * Math.PI / 180;\r\n\r\n  const a =\r\n    Math.sin(dLat / 2) ** 2 +\r\n    Math.cos(lat1 * Math.PI / 180) *\r\n    Math.cos(lat2 * Math.PI / 180) *\r\n    Math.sin(dLon / 2) ** 2;\r\n\r\n  const c = 2 * Math.atan2(\r\n    Math.sqrt(a),\r\n    Math.sqrt(1 - a)\r\n  );\r\n\r\n  return R * c;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 9.4 Allocation Algorithm\r\n\r\n1. Receive patient coordinates.\r\n2. Receive the required clinical department.\r\n3. Retrieve the hospital registry.\r\n4. Match registered specialties.\r\n5. Exclude unsuitable hospitals.\r\n6. Calculate straight-line distance.\r\n7. Sort eligible hospitals.\r\n8. Select the nearest suitable hospital.\r\n9. Return the selected hospital and distance.\r\n\r\nIf no appropriate hospital is available, return a safe fallback rather than assigning an unrelated hospital.\r\n\r\nClearly label distance as geographical straight-line distance, not road distance.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 10 \342\200\224 CORE FEATURE 5: 2.5-SECOND SOS EMERGENCY SYSTEM\r\n\r\n## 10.1 Purpose\r\n\r\nImplement an immediately accessible emergency control.\r\n\r\nThe patient must be able to trigger an SOS event without using voice recognition or waiting for Gemini.\r\n\r\n## 10.2 Native SOS Interface\r\n\r\nUse a large circular red Pressable control in the bottom navigation area.\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\n\r\n- Red emergency button.\r\n- Hold progress ring.\r\n- Haptic feedback.\r\n- Clear activation instruction.\r\n- Activation countdown.\r\n- Emergency confirmation.\r\n- Live SOS status.\r\n\r\n## 10.3 Exact Timing\r\n\r\nThe sequence must preserve these values:\r\n\r\n| Stage | Duration |\r\n|---|---:|\r\n| Intentional SOS hold | 2.5 seconds |\r\n| Local siren | 10 seconds |\r\n| Ambient recording | 20 seconds |\r\n\r\nThe backend SOS event must be submitted immediately after the 2.5-second hold succeeds.\r\n\r\nDo not wait 30 additional seconds before notifying the dashboard.\r\n\r\n## 10.4 State Machine\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\ntype SOSState =\r\n  | \"IDLE\"\r\n  | \"HOLDING\"\r\n  | \"SIREN\"\r\n  | \"RECORDING\"\r\n  | \"UPLOADING\"\r\n  | \"DISPATCHED\"\r\n  | \"FAILED\";\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 10.5 Activation Logic\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n\r\n- Press starts hold.\r\n- Display progress.\r\n- Release before 2.5 seconds cancels activation.\r\n- At 2.5 seconds activate SOS.\r\n- Trigger haptic feedback.\r\n- Capture GPS.\r\n- Send Priority 0 event.\r\n- Start local siren.\r\n- Record ambient audio.\r\n- Upload recording.\r\n- Update SOS ticket.\r\n\r\nUse native APIs:\r\n\r\n- React Native Pressable.\r\n- Expo Haptics.\r\n- Expo Location.\r\n- Expo Audio.\r\n- Native bundled audio asset.\r\n\r\nDo not use:\r\n\r\n- navigator.vibrate.\r\n- navigator.geolocation.\r\n- Web Audio API.\r\n- MediaRecorder.\r\n- Browser event handlers.\r\n\r\n## 10.6 Emergency API\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /api/v1/sos-dispatch\r\n```\r\n\r\nPayload:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"lat\": 17.7124,\r\n  \"lng\": 83.3156,\r\n  \"priority\": 0\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nResponse:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"success\": true,\r\n  \"sos_id\": \"SOS-001\",\r\n  \"status\": \"received\",\r\n  \"priority\": 0\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nUse server-generated IDs.\r\n\r\nThe endpoint must:\r\n\r\n- Validate coordinates.\r\n- Authenticate the patient.\r\n- Create a unique emergency record.\r\n- Set Priority 0.\r\n- Persist the event.\r\n- Trigger dashboard updates.\r\n- Return a valid SOS ticket ID.\r\n\r\nImplement an idempotency mechanism to prevent duplicate emergency records from repeated requests.\r\n\r\n## 10.7 Local Siren\r\n\r\nUse a locally bundled audio file.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Ten-second playback.\r\n- Audio cleanup.\r\n- Handle interruption.\r\n- Respect platform audio rules.\r\n- Provide a visual fallback when audio is unavailable.\r\n\r\nThe siren is a local device alert, not proof that emergency services have been contacted.\r\n\r\n## 10.8 Ambient Audio\r\n\r\nRecord for 20 seconds after the siren.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Request microphone permission.\r\n- Explain recording purpose.\r\n- Record audio.\r\n- Upload through a separate authenticated endpoint.\r\n- Associate audio with the SOS ticket.\r\n- Store the file securely.\r\n- Update SOS record.\r\n- Release audio resources.\r\n\r\nIf permission is denied or upload fails, preserve the SOS event and communicate the failure. Never cancel an already submitted emergency event because audio recording failed.\r\n\r\n## 10.9 Real Emergency Dispatch\r\n\r\nFor the prototype, implement a demo dispatch event and clearly label it as simulated.\r\n\r\nDo not claim an ambulance has been dispatched without an authorized, functioning emergency-service integration.\r\n\r\nOptional Twilio integration may support authorized SMS or callback notifications, but does not itself dispatch ambulances.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 11 \342\200\224 GEMINI MULTIMODAL AI ENGINE\r\n\r\n## 11.1 Model Architecture\r\n\r\nCreate a centralized Gemini provider.\r\n\r\nThe backend must handle:\r\n\r\n- Audio input.\r\n- Prescription images.\r\n- Symptom extraction.\r\n- Language detection.\r\n- Structured output.\r\n- Error handling.\r\n- Model selection.\r\n\r\nUse the currently supported Google Gen AI SDK.\r\n\r\nKeep the model ID configurable.\r\n\r\n## 11.2 AI Processing Flow\r\n\r\nAudio/Image Upload\r\n\342\206\223\r\nFile Validation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nGemini Multimodal Processing\r\n\342\206\223\r\nStructured JSON Response\r\n\342\206\223\r\nSchema Validation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nClinical Safety Validation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nHospital Allocation\r\n\342\206\223\r\nDatabase Persistence\r\n\342\206\223\r\nPatient Response\r\n\r\nThe AI must never directly control database writes or assign arbitrary hospital IDs.\r\n\r\n## 11.3 Structured Triage Response\r\n\r\nUse a schema similar to:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"success\",\r\n  \"tier\": 2,\r\n  \"translated_symptoms\": \"Persistent abdominal discomfort\",\r\n  \"detected_language\": \"te\",\r\n  \"clinical_department\": \"General Medicine\",\r\n  \"severity_score\": 6,\r\n  \"patient_instructions_native\": \"Patient instructions\",\r\n  \"safety_warning\": \"\",\r\n  \"requires_human_assessment\": true\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nHospital allocation should be completed by the backend after validating the AI response.\r\n\r\n## 11.4 Master System Prompt\r\n\r\nUse the following AI system instruction:\r\n\r\n\"You are Sanjeevani Triage, an AI-assisted multimodal healthcare routing assistant.\r\n\r\nYour job is to understand patient-reported symptoms, interpret medical documents when sufficiently legible, and provide structured information for a healthcare routing system.\r\n\r\nYou are not a doctor and must not independently diagnose diseases.\r\n\r\nLANGUAGE:\r\nSupport Telugu, Hindi, and English.\r\nDetect the language of patient audio.\r\nUnderstand natural speech and regional variations.\r\nTranslate symptoms into English for hospital staff.\r\nProvide patient-facing communication in the detected language.\r\n\r\nSYMPTOM EXTRACTION:\r\nExtract only information supported by patient input.\r\nDo not invent symptoms, medical history, or duration.\r\nIdentify missing information and uncertainty.\r\nFlag potential emergency warning signs.\r\n\r\nTIER 1:\r\nRecommend conservative self-care guidance only for clearly mild symptoms without warning signs.\r\nInclude a medical disclaimer and escalation instructions.\r\n\r\nTIER 2:\r\nIdentify the relevant clinical department and recommend clinical evaluation.\r\nDo not independently assign a hospital.\r\n\r\nTIER 3:\r\nIdentify potentially life-threatening symptoms.\r\nSet severity score to 10.\r\nRecommend immediate emergency assistance.\r\nDo not delay emergency instructions.\r\n\r\nPRESCRIPTION SCANNING:\r\nExtract only clearly legible medicine names, dosage, frequency, and duration.\r\nNever guess missing information.\r\nNever invent medication instructions.\r\nIf handwriting is ambiguous or unclear, abort extraction.\r\n\r\nReturn the exact warning:\r\nMedicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\r\n\r\nHOSPITAL ROUTING:\r\nDo not invent hospital IDs, hospital names, specialties, availability, or distances.\r\nThe backend will perform geographical calculations and final hospital allocation.\r\n\r\nOUTPUT:\r\nReturn valid JSON matching the supplied response schema.\r\nNever provide unsupported medical claims.\r\nNever claim that an ambulance or medical professional has been dispatched unless the backend confirms the relevant integration.\"\r\n\r\n## 11.5 AI Provider Reliability\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n\r\n- API timeout.\r\n- Retry with bounded attempts.\r\n- Rate limiting.\r\n- Error classification.\r\n- Model fallback configuration.\r\n- Response schema validation.\r\n- Logging without exposing patient data.\r\n- Safe handling of malformed AI output.\r\n\r\nIf Gemini is unavailable, provide an appropriate fallback and emergency instructions.\r\n\r\nNever silently downgrade an emergency to Tier 1 because the AI failed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 12 \342\200\224 BACKEND AND DATABASE ARCHITECTURE\r\n\r\n## 12.1 Backend Design\r\n\r\nBuild a modular Express application.\r\n\r\nSeparate:\r\n\r\n- Routes.\r\n- Controllers.\r\n- Services.\r\n- Repositories.\r\n- AI provider.\r\n- Authentication.\r\n- Validation.\r\n- Database access.\r\n- File storage.\r\n- Real-time events.\r\n\r\nDo not place all business logic in a single server file.\r\n\r\n## 12.2 PostgreSQL Database\r\n\r\nUse PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM.\r\n\r\nCreate the following entities:\r\n\r\n### Users\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- name.\r\n- phone.\r\n- email, optional.\r\n- password hash or external identity.\r\n- preferred language.\r\n- role.\r\n- created_at.\r\n- updated_at.\r\n\r\n### Patient Profiles\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- user_id.\r\n- date of birth, where necessary.\r\n- emergency contact.\r\n- relevant patient-provided medical information.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### Triage Records\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- patient_id.\r\n- detected_language.\r\n- translated_symptoms.\r\n- tier.\r\n- severity_score.\r\n- clinical_department.\r\n- status.\r\n- safety_warning.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### Hospitals\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- hospital_name.\r\n- address.\r\n- latitude.\r\n- longitude.\r\n- specialties.\r\n- registration status.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### OPD Tokens\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- patient_id.\r\n- triage_id.\r\n- hospital_id.\r\n- token_number.\r\n- department.\r\n- status.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### SOS Events\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- patient_id.\r\n- latitude.\r\n- longitude.\r\n- priority.\r\n- status.\r\n- ambient_audio_url.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### Prescriptions\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- patient_id.\r\n- image_url.\r\n- extraction_status.\r\n- extracted_data.\r\n- safety_warning.\r\n- created_at.\r\n\r\n### Audit Logs\r\n\r\n- id.\r\n- actor_id.\r\n- action.\r\n- resource_type.\r\n- resource_id.\r\n- timestamp.\r\n\r\nImplement foreign keys, indexes, unique constraints, and appropriate access controls.\r\n\r\nUse database transactions for token generation and important queue changes.\r\n\r\n## 12.3 Data Storage\r\n\r\nDo not use serverless local JSON files as permanent production storage.\r\n\r\nUse:\r\n\r\n- PostgreSQL for structured records.\r\n- Object storage for audio and image files.\r\n- Secure signed URLs for authorized media access.\r\n- Appropriate retention and deletion policies.\r\n\r\nFor local development, provide seed data.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 13 \342\200\224 COMPLETE API SPECIFICATION\r\n\r\nCreate versioned API routes.\r\n\r\nBase URL:\r\n\r\n```text\r\n/api/v1\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Authentication\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /auth/register\r\nPOST /auth/login\r\nPOST /auth/logout\r\nGET  /auth/me\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Patient\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGET   /patients/me\r\nPATCH /patients/me\r\nGET   /patients/me/history\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Triage\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /triage\r\nGET  /triage/:id\r\nGET  /triage/history\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Prescription\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /prescriptions/scan\r\nGET  /prescriptions\r\nGET  /prescriptions/:id\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Hospitals\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGET /hospitals\r\nGET /hospitals/:id\r\nPOST /hospitals/recommend\r\n```\r\n\r\n### OPD Tokens\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST  /tokens\r\nGET   /tokens\r\nGET   /tokens/:id\r\nPATCH /tokens/:id/status\r\n```\r\n\r\n### SOS\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /sos-dispatch\r\nPOST /sos/:id/context\r\nGET  /sos/:id\r\nGET  /sos/history\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Admin\r\n\r\n```text\r\nGET   /admin/dashboard\r\nGET   /admin/patients\r\nGET   /admin/queue\r\nGET   /admin/emergencies\r\nPATCH /admin/queue/:id/status\r\nPOST  /admin/patients/:id/callback\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Health Insights\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPOST /health-insights\r\nGET  /health-insights\r\n```\r\n\r\nAll endpoints must have authentication and role-based authorization appropriate to their operation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# PART 14 \342\200\224 HOSPITAL ADMIN DASHBOARD\r\n\r\n## 14.1 Purpose\r\n\r\nBuild a separate desktop web dashboard for hospital receptionists and authorized healthcare staff.\r\n\r\nThe dashboard must receive actual patient records from the central backend.\r\n\r\nIt must not use unrelated hardcoded patient data as its primary operating mode.\r\n\r\n## 14.2 Main Dashboard\r\n\r\nDisplay:\r\n\r\n- Hospital branding.\r\n- Hospital name.\r\n- Current date.\r\n- Total patients.\r\n- Active queue.\r\n- Emergency cases.\r"
    num_lines: 2413
