  planner_response {
    response: "# Sanjeevani Triage: Product Implementation Summary\n\nWe have built and verified **Sanjeevani Triage** as a multimodal healthcare triage and priority-based hospital queue management platform. The platform connects the patient-facing mobile application with a central full-stack backend orchestration gateway powered by Google Gemini and an operational hospital admin dashboard.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n#### 1. Voice-to-Token OPD (Core Feature 1)\n- **Zero-UI Natural Speech Interaction**: Large circular microphone with gesture handling, animated audio waveform, live recording timer, and cancel controls.\n- **Multilingual Multimodal Processing**: Interprets Telugu, Hindi, and English symptoms via Gemini (`gemini-3.8-flash`), extracts clinical complaints, translates symptoms into professional English for hospital clinicians, and provides patient instructions in their detected native language.\n- **Digital OPD Token Generation**: Concurrency-safe token numbering (`OPD-101`, `OPD-102`...), assigned specialty department, wait-time estimation, and QR verification badge.\n\n#### 2. Smart Rx Decoder (Core Feature 2)\n- **Camera Viewfinder & Capture Interface**: Supports image capture, file upload, and preloaded sample testing.\n- **Strict Clinical Prescription Safety Protocol**: System enforces zero guesswork on medicine names, dosages, frequencies, and durations. When handwriting is illegible, smudged, or ambiguous, extraction aborts and returns the exact safety warning:  \n  *`\"Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\"`*\n\n#### 3. Three-Tier Intelligent Triage & Hospital Allocation (Core Features 3 & 4)\n- **Tier 1 (Self-Care)**: Conservative guidance in native language + medical disclaimer. Excluded from the hospital queue.\n- **Tier 2 (OPD Consultation)**: Clinical evaluation matched with registered hospitals using Haversine straight-line distance calculation (`calculateDistance`) against the Visakhapatnam hospital registry (Apollo Hospitals, CARE Hospitals, Medicover Hospital, Icon Krishi KIMS).\n- **Tier 3 (Emergency)**: Life-threatening symptom identification, severity score 10, immediate escalation guidance.\n\n#### 4. 2.5-Second SOS Emergency System (Core Feature 5)\n- **Exact Timing & State Machine**:\n  - **2.5s Intentional Hold**: Progress ring countdown; releasing under 2.5s cancels cleanly back to `IDLE`.\n  - **Immediate Priority 0 Dispatch**: As soon as the 2.5s threshold is reached, sends GPS coordinates to `POST /api/v1/sos-dispatch` with server-generated ID (`SOS-001`).\n  - **10-Second Local Siren**: Synthesized audio frequency-sweeping oscillator alert (750 Hz\342\200\2231150 Hz) and haptic feedback.\n  - **20-Second Ambient Recording**: Captures audio environment after the siren and associates it with the active SOS ticket.\n\n#### 5. Hospital Admin Priority Dashboard\n- **Dynamic Severity-Ranked Queue**: Replaces simple FIFO queues:\n  1. **Priority 0 SOS Cards**: Displayed at the very top with ticket ID, GPS coordinates, Google Maps link, 20s ambient audio player, and a 1-click **CALLBACK PATIENT** modal.\n  2. **Tier 3 Emergency Cards**: Red-bordered priority cards with severity 10 and clinical symptom summaries.\n  3. **Tier 2 OPD Cards**: Ordered by severity score (4\342\200\2238) with live status management (*Waiting*, *In Consultation*, *Completed*).\n  4. **Tier 1 Excluded**: Self-care cases kept out of the clinical queue.\n- **Real-Time Live Updates**: Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming updates across mobile actions and the hospital command center.\n\n#### 6. Interactive Dual-Screen Simulation & Monorepo Hub\n- **Split Simulation View**: Allows testing Voice Triage or triggering an SOS on the mobile app (left) and immediately watching the record appear at the top of the hospital queue (right).\n- **Monorepo Code Inspector**: Native React Native / Expo source files, PostgreSQL Prisma schema, and EAS build configuration (`eas build -p android --profile preview`)."
    modified_response: "# Sanjeevani Triage: Product Implementation Summary\n\nWe have built and verified **Sanjeevani Triage** as a multimodal healthcare triage and priority-based hospital queue management platform. The platform connects the patient-facing mobile application with a central full-stack backend orchestration gateway powered by Google Gemini and an operational hospital admin dashboard.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n#### 1. Voice-to-Token OPD (Core Feature 1)\n- **Zero-UI Natural Speech Interaction**: Large circular microphone with gesture handling, animated audio waveform, live recording timer, and cancel controls.\n- **Multilingual Multimodal Processing**: Interprets Telugu, Hindi, and English symptoms via Gemini (`gemini-3.8-flash`), extracts clinical complaints, translates symptoms into professional English for hospital clinicians, and provides patient instructions in their detected native language.\n- **Digital OPD Token Generation**: Concurrency-safe token numbering (`OPD-101`, `OPD-102`...), assigned specialty department, wait-time estimation, and QR verification badge.\n\n#### 2. Smart Rx Decoder (Core Feature 2)\n- **Camera Viewfinder & Capture Interface**: Supports image capture, file upload, and preloaded sample testing.\n- **Strict Clinical Prescription Safety Protocol**: System enforces zero guesswork on medicine names, dosages, frequencies, and durations. When handwriting is illegible, smudged, or ambiguous, extraction aborts and returns the exact safety warning:  \n  *`\"Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\"`*\n\n#### 3. Three-Tier Intelligent Triage & Hospital Allocation (Core Features 3 & 4)\n- **Tier 1 (Self-Care)**: Conservative guidance in native language + medical disclaimer. Excluded from the hospital queue.\n- **Tier 2 (OPD Consultation)**: Clinical evaluation matched with registered hospitals using Haversine straight-line distance calculation (`calculateDistance`) against the Visakhapatnam hospital registry (Apollo Hospitals, CARE Hospitals, Medicover Hospital, Icon Krishi KIMS).\n- **Tier 3 (Emergency)**: Life-threatening symptom identification, severity score 10, immediate escalation guidance.\n\n#### 4. 2.5-Second SOS Emergency System (Core Feature 5)\n- **Exact Timing & State Machine**:\n  - **2.5s Intentional Hold**: Progress ring countdown; releasing under 2.5s cancels cleanly back to `IDLE`.\n  - **Immediate Priority 0 Dispatch**: As soon as the 2.5s threshold is reached, sends GPS coordinates to `POST /api/v1/sos-dispatch` with server-generated ID (`SOS-001`).\n  - **10-Second Local Siren**: Synthesized audio frequency-sweeping oscillator alert (750 Hz\342\200\2231150 Hz) and haptic feedback.\n  - **20-Second Ambient Recording**: Captures audio environment after the siren and associates it with the active SOS ticket.\n\n#### 5. Hospital Admin Priority Dashboard\n- **Dynamic Severity-Ranked Queue**: Replaces simple FIFO queues:\n  1. **Priority 0 SOS Cards**: Displayed at the very top with ticket ID, GPS coordinates, Google Maps link, 20s ambient audio player, and a 1-click **CALLBACK PATIENT** modal.\n  2. **Tier 3 Emergency Cards**: Red-bordered priority cards with severity 10 and clinical symptom summaries.\n  3. **Tier 2 OPD Cards**: Ordered by severity score (4\342\200\2238) with live status management (*Waiting*, *In Consultation*, *Completed*).\n  4. **Tier 1 Excluded**: Self-care cases kept out of the clinical queue.\n- **Real-Time Live Updates**: Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming updates across mobile actions and the hospital command center.\n\n#### 6. Interactive Dual-Screen Simulation & Monorepo Hub\n- **Split Simulation View**: Allows testing Voice Triage or triggering an SOS on the mobile app (left) and immediately watching the record appear at the top of the hospital queue (right).\n- **Monorepo Code Inspector**: Native React Native / Expo source files, PostgreSQL Prisma schema, and EAS build configuration (`eas build -p android --profile preview`)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\240\003\n\235\003\001i\024}\023\373s\204K\357e\004\317rp\267\r\255h\373\")\375a\236([\253\001\317\375\323~E(~\035\227}\322\341\241\230\325G\346\314%,\365\276\021\233M\324\2511\017\331\253e;\356\017\217\220\212\274\343\212:\362\217\313\350d#\003\372.u\314\327\207E\303\222\247\327\v\204\325\223$\271\020wH#\342\300?@\230\026\361,\256r\213\263\252Kd{\273(\372y\265\037\247=>\001!A\351\365\247\t\312\271)\3410\216\a\272\005\215\345\240x(-}m`@\322=\"(>\237\335\r_N\036\223<\250\362&\314A\253\275\257\326\020\277\177\3259\237E\270T]\340\211\205\340G\367\332\354\r9x\201d\270\016\310\214\367\260l\376P\260\313=\217,%\205Tj\360\200\232t\216p\364\344\364\335<C\225\030e\223\245\203\207\001\017\205\216\211`%s}`1O\243\255>*\200\331\254\255\276\207\375E\224$\311\302g\r\336I\270\026\001HT\246G\273\265\322\362gT\264\345\306Z\225*\247\240\334\276\322\225\274\003\354\035\264s\361\230\340\202\204\373\222\357\016}\253Oz\374XB\354E\346\b\375\nE\367\311.\334\217\177\360S\312\331\374A\325l\345\367\355\023D;\ab;\337m\366\035\357\372\216\337a\352\361\216\201-l6\242\241\003\\W\277\r\305\026\363\r\327+\021\204\001\v\021{bO\231\374\005\312\3229=x\016\245\027\256\252\335\212\362\302 @\001\213)\336\330a\234\r\276\270r\324]\377\211\224"
