  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/live_api.md"
    end_line: 345
    content: "# Gemini Live API \342\200\224 Real-Time Voice & Video (`@google/genai`)\n\n> All `@google/genai` calls below run **server-side** using the shared\n> `GoogleGenAI` client initialized with `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` and\n> `\'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\'` (see `SKILL.md`).\n\nThe Live API enables low-latency, real-time voice interactions with Gemini. The\nserver manages the Live API session; audio streams between the client and server\nvia WebSocket.\n\n## Session Setup & Audio Streaming\n\nServer (`server.ts`): connects to Gemini Live and bridges audio via WebSocket.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, LiveServerMessage, Modality } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { WebSocketServer } from \"ws\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nwss.on(\"connection\", async (clientWs) => {\n  const session = await ai.live.connect({\n    model: \"gemini-3.8-live\",\n    config: {\n      responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],\n      speechConfig: {\n        // \'Puck\', \'Charon\', \'Kore\', \'Fenrir\', \'Zephyr\'\n        voiceConfig: { prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName: \"Zephyr\" } },\n      },\n      systemInstruction: \"You are a helpful assistant.\",\n    },\n    callbacks: {\n      onmessage: (message: LiveServerMessage) => {\n        for (const part of message.serverContent?.modelTurn?.parts ?? []) {\n          if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n            clientWs.send(JSON.stringify({ audio: part.inlineData.data }));\n          }\n        }\n        if (message.serverContent?.interrupted) {\n          clientWs.send(JSON.stringify({ interrupted: true }));\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  });\n\n  clientWs.on(\"message\", (data) => {\n    const { audio } = JSON.parse(data.toString());\n    session.sendRealtimeInput({\n      audio: { data: audio, mimeType: \"audio/pcm;rate=16000\" },\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\nClient (browser): captures mic audio and plays back responses.\n\n```ts\nconst ws = new WebSocket(`ws://${location.host}/live`);\n// Input: 16kHz for mic capture\nconst inputAudioCtx = new AudioContext({ sampleRate: 16000 });\n// Output: 24kHz for model output playback\nconst outputAudioCtx = new AudioContext({ sampleRate: 24000 });\n\nconst stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true });\nconst source = inputAudioCtx.createMediaStreamSource(stream);\nconst processor = inputAudioCtx.createScriptProcessor(4096, 1, 1);\nsource.connect(processor);\nprocessor.connect(inputAudioCtx.destination);\n\nprocessor.onaudioprocess = (e) => {\n  const base64 = pcmToBase64(e.inputBuffer.getChannelData(0));\n  ws.send(JSON.stringify({ audio: base64 }));\n};\n\nws.onmessage = (event) => {\n  const msg = JSON.parse(event.data);\n  // Play back at 24kHz\n  if (msg.audio) playAudioChunk(outputAudioCtx, msg.audio);\n  if (msg.interrupted) { /* stop playback, clear queue */ }\n};\n```\n\n## Extended Thinking in Live\n\nUse `gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking` (requires `@google/genai` `>= 2.25.0`)\nwhen real-time voice conversations require complex reasoning, high-precision\ndecision-making, or multi-step tool calls:\n\n1.  **Thinking level:** Set `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel` to\n    `ThinkingLevel.LOW`, `ThinkingLevel.MEDIUM`, or `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`.\n    `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL` is **not** supported. (Do **not** set\n    `thinkingConfig` on `gemini-3.8-live`.)\n2.  **Non-blocking tools required:** Every `FunctionDeclaration` in `tools`\n    **must** set `behavior: Behavior.NON_BLOCKING` so tools run asynchronously\n    while the model streams spoken updates. Synchronous blocking tools return an\n    error.\n3.  **Track `interactionStatus` instead of `turnComplete`:** Because the model\n    emits intermediate spoken fillers (each ending with `turnComplete: true`)\n    while background reasoning or tools are still running, inspect\n    `message.serverContent?.interactionStatus` (`InteractionStatus.IN_PROGRESS`\n    vs. `InteractionStatus.IDLE`) to manage overall session/UI state.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  Behavior,\n  FunctionDeclaration,\n  FunctionResponseScheduling,\n  GoogleGenAI,\n  InteractionStatus,\n  LiveServerMessage,\n  Modality,\n  ThinkingLevel,\n  Type,\n} from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst searchDocs: FunctionDeclaration = {\n  name: \"searchDocs\",\n  description: \"Searches reference documentation asynchronously.\",\n  behavior: Behavior.NON_BLOCKING,\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      query: { type: Type.STRING },\n    },\n    required: [\"query\"],\n  },\n};\n\nconst session = await ai.live.connect({\n  model: \"gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking\",\n  config: {\n    responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],\n    thinkingConfig: {\n      thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.HIGH,\n    },\n    tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [searchDocs] }],\n    systemInstruction: \"You are an interactive coding coach.\",\n  },\n  callbacks: {\n    onmessage: (message: LiveServerMessage) => {\n      for (const part of message.serverContent?.modelTurn?.parts ?? []) {\n        if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n          // Handle 24kHz PCM audio chunk\n        }\n      }\n      for (const call of message.toolCall?.functionCalls ?? []) {\n        session.sendToolResponse({\n          functionResponses: [{\n            id: call.id,\n            name: call.name,\n            response: { result: \"Found matching docs\" },\n            scheduling: FunctionResponseScheduling.WHEN_IDLE, // or INTERRUPT | SILENT\n          }],\n        });\n      }\n      const status = message.serverContent?.interactionStatus;\n      if (status === InteractionStatus.IN_PROGRESS) {\n        // Model is still reasoning or awaiting non-blocking tool responses\n      } else if (status === InteractionStatus.IDLE) {\n        // All reasoning and tool turns complete; ready for next user input\n      }\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Live Translation & Live Transcription\n\nLive speech-to-speech translation and live speech-to-text transcription use two\ndistinct specialized Live API models:\n\n### Live Speech-to-Speech Translation (`gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview`)\n\nUse `gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview` for low-latency, real-time\nspeech-to-speech translation across 70+ languages. Configure `translationConfig`\nwith `responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO]`.\n\n> **Important:** `gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview` operates as a dedicated\n> interpreter pipeline\342\200\224do **not** pass `systemInstruction`, `tools`, or\n> text/video inputs (only 16kHz PCM audio input is supported).\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, LiveServerMessage, Modality } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { WebSocketServer } from \"ws\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nwss.on(\"connection\", async (clientWs) => {\n  const session = await ai.live.connect({\n    model: \"gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview\",\n    config: {\n      responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],\n      inputAudioTranscription: {},\n      outputAudioTranscription: {},\n      translationConfig: {\n        targetLanguageCode: \"es\", // Translates spoken input audio into Spanish\n        echoTargetLanguage: false, // Default false: do not parrot target-language input\n      },\n    },\n    callbacks: {\n      onmessage: (message: LiveServerMessage) => {\n        const content = message.serverContent;\n        if (content?.inputTranscription?.text) {\n          clientWs.send(\n            JSON.stringify({ inputTranscript: content.inputTranscription.text })\n          );\n        }\n        if (content?.outputTranscription?.text) {\n          clientWs.send(\n            JSON.stringify({\n              outputTranscript: content.outputTranscription.text,\n            })\n          );\n        }\n        for (const part of content?.modelTurn?.parts ?? []) {\n          if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n            clientWs.send(JSON.stringify({ audio: part.inlineData.data }));\n          }\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  });\n\n  clientWs.on(\"message\", (data) => {\n    const { audio } = JSON.parse(data.toString());\n    session.sendRealtimeInput({\n      audio: { data: audio, mimeType: \"audio/pcm;rate=16000\" },\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Live Audio Transcription (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`)\n\nUse `gemini-3.5-transcribe-live` for real-time streaming speech-to-text\ntranscription. Set `responseModalities: [Modality.TEXT]` and configure\n`inputAudioTranscription`:\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI, LiveServerMessage, Modality } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { WebSocketServer } from \"ws\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nwss.on(\"connection\", async (clientWs) => {\n  const session = await ai.live.connect({\n    model: \"gemini-3.5-transcribe-live\",\n    config: {\n      responseModalities: [Modality.TEXT],\n      inputAudioTranscription: {\n        languageCodes: [], // Empty or omitted for automatic language detection\n      },\n    },\n    callbacks: {\n      onmessage: (message: LiveServerMessage) => {\n        const content = message.serverContent;\n        if (content?.interimInputTranscription?.text) {\n          clientWs.send(\n            JSON.stringify({\n              interimTranscript: content.interimInputTranscription.text,\n            })\n          );\n        }\n        if (content?.inputTranscription?.text) {\n          clientWs.send(\n            JSON.stringify({ transcript: content.inputTranscription.text })\n          );\n        }\n      },\n    },\n  });\n\n  clientWs.on(\"message\", (data) => {\n    const { audio } = JSON.parse(data.toString());\n    session.sendRealtimeInput({\n      audio: { data: audio, mimeType: \"audio/pcm;rate=16000\" },\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Video Streaming\n\nStream image frames received from the client as separate inputs.\n\n```ts\nsession.sendRealtimeInput(\n  { video: { data: base64Data, mimeType: \'image/jpeg\' } });\n```\n\n## Audio Transcription\n\nEnable transcription in config:\n\n```ts\nconfig: {\n  // ...\n  outputAudioTranscription: {}, // Model output\n  inputAudioTranscription: {}, // User input\n}\n```\n\nHandle `outputTranscription` and `inputTranscription` in `onmessage`.\n\n## Function Calling in Live\n\nDefine tools in config and handle `toolCall` in `onmessage`. Send\n`functionResponses` back using `session.sendToolResponse`.\n\n## Live API Rules\n\n-   **Streaming Input:** When sending data via `session.sendRealtimeInput`, use\n    `audio`, `video`, or `text` fields. The `media` and `mediaChunks` fields are\n    **deprecated** and **must not** be used.\n    -   **Correct:** `session.sendRealtimeInput({ audio: ... })`\n    -   **Correct:** `session.sendRealtimeInput({ video: ... })`\n    -   **Incorrect:** `session.sendRealtimeInput({ media: ... })`\n-   **Audio Sync:** Schedule audio chunks precisely for gapless playback. Track\n    a `nextStartTime` and use `AudioBufferSourceNode.start(nextStartTime)` for\n    each chunk, advancing by `buffer.duration`. Do not play chunks immediately\n    on arrival \342\200\224 network jitter causes overlaps and gaps.\n-   **Cleanup:** Use `session.close()` when finished.\n-   **Modalities:** `responseModalities` must be `[Modality.AUDIO]` for voice\n    and speech-translation sessions (`gemini-3.8-live`,\n    `gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking`, `gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview`),\n    or `[Modality.TEXT]` for dedicated live speech-to-text transcription\n    (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`).\n-   **Raw Audio:** Implement manual PCM encoding/decoding. Do not use\n    `AudioContext.decodeAudioData` on raw streams.\n-   **Session State:** Use `sessionPromise.then(...)` to send data to avoid race\n    conditions and stale closures.\n-   **Callback State (React):** In React, use `useRef` (not `useState`) for any\n    variable accessed inside `onaudioprocess` or `setInterval` callbacks to\n    avoid stale closures.\n-   **Video:** Send synchronized image frames and audio.\n-   **Multimodal Output:** Always handle audio output, even when transcription\n    or function calls are enabled.\n-   **Audio Formats:** Live API requires raw 16-bit PCM little-endian audio.\n    Input audio must be 16kHz (`audio/pcm;rate=16000`), and model output audio\n    is 24kHz. Ensure the client handles this (e.g., by using a separate 24kHz\n    `AudioContext` for playback to avoid pitch-shifting or slow playback).\n-   **Video Input Rate:** When streaming video/images, send JPEG frames at a\n    rate of at most 1 frame per second (1 FPS) to avoid overwhelming the model.\n"
