  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Integration**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. First, there\'s a problem with AI health chat integration. Secondly, the user needs chat history implemented. I\'m focusing on those two key issues for a solution.\n\n\n**Implementing Chat History Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on chat history. The objective is instant retrieval and continuation of multi-turn threads, which will need storage in Firestore or a backend solution. I also understand that the user language will change completely. It seems that complete internationalization and localization across the entire application in several languages, along with the chatbot, are required for the new features.\n\n\n**Defining Localization Dictionary**\n\nI\'m now focused on the foundational work for internationalization. I\'m building a localization dictionary in `src/utils/translations.ts`, specifically for Telugu, Hindi, and English. This will cover the entire application, including the global header, view switcher, mobile status, daily insights, voice triage, smart Rx decoder, SOS button, OPD tokens, and health records.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the scope to cover triage history, prescriptions, SOS logs, and the \"no records\" message. I\'m also considering the patient profile, the bottom navigation bar, and the Hospital Admin Dashboard, including its command center, live queue, and emergency management. A crucial aspect is the chatbot modal and live voice modal with features like roles, model pickers, and chat history. Also, I\'m working on a React `LanguageContext` to ensure instant app-wide language synchronization.\n\n\n**Refining Chat Implementation**\n\nI\'m now revising the chat feature\'s presentation. Instead of a dedicated tab, it\'ll be a button-triggered popup. I\'m focusing on features such as chat history with instant retrieval and continuation, proper markdown rendering, and symptom extraction. The goal is to make multi-turn chat persistence in Firestore, with endpoints to retrieve and manage conversations.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
