  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Prompt/Task**:\n  1. \"AI health chat is not integrated properly.\" Fix integration and ensure high usability with multi-turn chat capabilities.\n  2. \"Also implement chat history.\" Provide persistent conversation history/sessions (save, list, resume, delete chat sessions).\n  3. \"Total Application language has to be changed when user changer his language.\" Implement full application-wide internationalization across Telugu (`te`), Hindi (`hi`), and English (`en`), so changing the language in the header or in the mobile view immediately updates every screen (Mobile Home, Tabs, Daily Health Insight, Voice-to-Token OPD, Smart Rx Decoder, 2.5s SOS Emergency, OPD Tokens, Health Records, Profile, Admin Dashboard, and Chatbot).\n- **Database Context**: User\'s Firestore database ID is `ai-studio-sanjeevanitriage-a37f31bb-2221-43e0-a139-6c5f97afa330` on Firebase Project `gen-lang-client-0659443606`.\n- **Target Applet ID**: `a37f31bb-2221-43e0-a139-6c5f97afa330`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  1. `src/utils/translations.ts`: Comprehensive translation dictionaries for Telugu (`te`), Hindi (`hi`), and English (`en`), covering headers, mobile CTAs, modals, OPD tokens, health insights, emergency SOS, and hospital admin dashboard.\n  2. `src/context/LanguageContext.tsx`: React Context and hook (`useLanguage`) managing the global language state with `localStorage` persistence and profile synchronization.\n  3. `src/services/chatStorage.ts`: Multi-turn chat session storage manager with Firestore persistence (`/chat_conversations/{sessionId}`) and local cache, supporting session listing, saving, and deletion.\n  4. `src/components/chat/GeminiChatbotModal.tsx`: Complete multi-turn chat interface with slide-out conversation history drawer, \"+ New Chat\" button, model switcher (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `gemini-4-argon`), role selection (General Guide, Clinical Specialist, Rapid Triage), quick question chips, and OPD token generation shortcut.\n  5. `firestore.rules`: Updated with `chat_conversations/{convId}` and subcollections; deployed via `deploy_firebase` tool (status: completed).\n  6. `firebase-blueprint.json`: Configured with `ChatMessage`, `UserProfile`, `TriageRecord`, `OPDToken`, `SOSEvent`, and collections.\n  7. `server.ts`: Includes full-stack Express routes, Vite middleware, and WebSocket server (`/api/live`) for `gemini-3.8-live` Live API voice streaming.\n  8. `src/server/gemini.ts` & `src/server/routes.ts`: `chatWithGemini` multi-turn chat function and `POST /api/v1/chat` endpoint supporting all three model choices.\n- **In Progress / Edits Remaining**:\n  - Wiring `useLanguage()` into the remaining UI components (`MobileAppView.tsx`, `DailyHealthInsightCard.tsx`, `VoiceTriageSheet.tsx`, `PrescriptionScannerSheet.tsx`, `SOSEmergencyButton.tsx`, `OPDTokensList.tsx`, `HealthRecordsView.tsx`, `HospitalAdminView.tsx`, and `App.tsx` main wrapper) so all labels pull from `t.*`.\n  - Adding a direct \"Chat\" tab or integrated button in `MobileAppView.tsx` navigation bar so the chat is a first-class feature of the patient mobile app.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- Cloud SQL feature eligibility returned `NO_VALID_PROJECT`, which per the `cloudsql-setup` skill strictly required pivoting silently to Firebase/Firestore.\n- Firebase provisioning was accepted by user and succeeded with project ID `gen-lang-client-0659443606` and database `ai-studio-sanjeevanitriage-a37f31bb-2221-43e0-a139-6c5f97afa330`.\n- The Live API requires raw 16kHz PCM input and 24kHz PCM output; WebSocket bridge is functional in `server.ts`.\n- Complete application internationalization requires wrapping root app components in `<LanguageProvider>` and referencing `t` from `useLanguage()`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. *Missing `PrescriptionRecord` import in `src/server/routes.ts`*:\n   - Error: `error TS2304: Cannot find name \'PrescriptionRecord\'`.\n   - Fix: Added `PrescriptionRecord` to the `../types` import list.\n2. *Missing bracket in `routes.ts` line 477*:\n   - Error: `error TS1005: \'}\' expected` after adding `/chat` route.\n   - Fix: Added missing closing bracket `});` to `router.get(\'/health-insights\')`.\n3. *Missing `Bot` import in `src/App.tsx`*:\n   - Error: TypeScript compile error for missing `Bot` icon.\n   - Fix: Added `Bot` to `lucide-react` import.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Server process runs `tsx server.ts` on port 3000.\n- Dev server is responsive and healthy (`curl http://localhost:3000/api/health` returns `status: \"healthy\", gemini_available: true`).\n- `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, and `gemini-4-argon` endpoints are tested and functional.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Wrap App in `LanguageProvider`**:\n   - Update `src/main.tsx` or `src/App.tsx` to wrap the entire application tree in `<LanguageProvider>`.\n2. **Apply `useLanguage()` across All Components**:\n   - `src/App.tsx`: Use `t.appTitle`, `t.dualScreenView`, `t.patientAppView`, `t.adminQueueView`, `t.liveVoiceBtn`, `t.aiChatBtn`, `t.servicesOperational`, etc.\n   - `src/components/mobile/MobileAppView.tsx`: Use `t.greeting(name)`, `t.greetingSubtitle`, `t.speakSymptomsTitle`, `t.smartRxTitle`, `t.liveVoiceTitle`, `t.aiChatTitle`, `t.navHome`, `t.navChat`, `t.navRecords`, `t.navTokens`, `t.navProfile`.\n   - Add a dedicated **Chat** tab in mobile bottom nav: Home, Chat, Central SOS, Records, Tokens, Profile.\n   - `src/components/mobile/DailyHealthInsightCard.tsx`: Use `t.dailyHealthInsight`, `t.steps`, `t.sleep`, `t.avgHeartRate`, `t.insightTip`.\n   - `src/components/mobile/VoiceTriageSheet.tsx`: Use `t.voiceTriageModalTitle`, `t.listeningSymptoms`, `t.analyzingGemini`, `t.tapToSpeak`, etc.\n   - `src/components/mobile/PrescriptionScannerSheet.tsx`: Use `t.rxModalTitle`, `t.snapOrUpload`, `t.takePhoto`, `t.safetyGuardrailTriggered`, etc.\n   - `src/components/mobile/SOSEmergencyButton.tsx`: Use `t.holdSosBtn`, `t.priority0Activated`, `t.emergencyDispatchLive`, etc.\n   - `src/components/mobile/OPDTokensList.tsx`: Use `t.activeOpdTokensTitle`, `t.noActiveTokens`, `t.issuedAt`, etc.\n   - `src/components/mobile/HealthRecordsView.tsx`: Use `t.healthRecordsTitle`, `t.triageRecordsTab`, `t.prescriptionsTab`, `t.sosLogsTab`.\n   - `src/components/admin/HospitalAdminView.tsx`: Use `t.adminCommandCenter`, `t.liveQueueBadge`, `t.totalPatientsToday`, `t.activeQueueCount`, `t.queueTableHeader`, `t.departmentFilterLabel`, `t.callbackPatientBtn`, `t.markResolvedBtn`.\n   - `src/components/live/GeminiLiveVoiceModal.tsx`: Use `t.liveVoiceModalTitle`, `t.liveVoiceListening`, `t.endConversationBtn`.\n3. **Verify Build & Run Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` concurrently.\n   - Restart dev server with `restart_dev_server` if server scripts change.\n   - Verify language toggle works across Telugu, Hindi, and English with zero untranslated hardcoded strings.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- The patient mobile app must feel like a native mobile app with Zero-UI design principles.\n- The hospital admin dashboard must prioritize patients strictly by clinical severity (Priority 0 SOS first, Tier 3 emergency second, Tier 2 OPD third, Tier 1 excluded).\n- Prescription safety protocol is absolute: if handwriting is unclear, extraction MUST stop with the exact warning: `\"Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\"`\n- The Live API must strictly use `gemini-3.8-live`.\n- Chatbot must use `gemini-4-argon` for complex tasks, `gemini-3.8-flash` for general tasks, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for fast tasks.\n- Keep `metadata.json` capabilities intact with `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 221
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
