  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining GeminiChatbotModal**\n\nI\'ve been diving into `GeminiChatbotModal.tsx`. It\'s impressive! Multi-turn conversations are handled seamlessly, with multi-model support \342\200\223 `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, and `gemini-4-argon` are all included. Plus, roles, a history drawer, Firestore synchronization, and copy functionality are all integrated, quite effectively.\n\n\n**Analyzing App Entrypoints**\n\nI\'m now examining `src/main.tsx` and `src/App.tsx`. I was surprised to see `LanguageProvider` isn\'t wrapping the `App` component in `main.tsx`. `App.tsx` itself has hardcoded text in the navigation, with no language switcher in the desktop header. Language changes within `MobileAppView` only update local state, not the entire app\'s context. This means language changes aren\'t propagating globally, a key oversight!\n\n\n**Identifying Language Integration**\n\nI\'ve circled back to `MobileAppView.tsx` and found a significant issue! The `handleLanguageChange` function updates the profile in the API but doesn\'t call `setLanguage(lang)` from `useLanguage()`. This disconnect means language changes aren\'t reflected across the app. Furthermore, I\'ve observed a multitude of hardcoded English labels within the view.\n\n\n"
