  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requests**\n\nI\'m now focused on dissecting the user\'s requirements. I\'ve identified three key areas: integrating the AI health chat feature correctly, implementing chat history functionality, and ensuring the application\'s language updates dynamically with the user\'s settings. I\'m prioritizing the integration aspect first.\n\n\n**Implementing Language Support**\n\nI\'m now breaking down language changes into concrete steps. I plan to wrap `<LanguageProvider>` around the application root. A global selector in the header will allow users to change languages, syncing with the mobile view\'s internal selector through `useLanguage()`. I will implement the calls to `setLanguage(lang)` in both locations.  Finally, I will ensure `MobileAppView.tsx` uses `t.*` for all translatable strings.\n\n\n**Identifying Translatable Strings**\n\nI\'m currently compiling the list of translatable strings, pulling them from several components. I\'ve pinpointed keys within AI chat cards, OPD token headers, ambulance helpline information, and various tabs like health records, tokens, and profile. I\'m also addressing the bottom navigation items and strings from `DailyHealthInsightCard.tsx` and `VoiceTriageSheet.tsx`. My goal is to create a comprehensive list for localization.\n\n\n**Expanding Translation Inventory**\n\nI\'m now expanding the translatable string inventory. I\'ve located several keys within `PrescriptionScannerSheet.tsx`, including strings related to the prescription scanning process and modal titles. I also identified translatable elements within `SOSEmergencyButton.tsx`, specifically regarding emergency dispatch and alert stages, and `OPDTokensList.tsx` related to active OPD tokens. Furthermore, I\'ve started the list with the addition of `HealthRecordsView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Compiling Localization Keys**\n\nI\'m now integrating more keys into the translation inventory. Specifically, I\'ve added strings from `HospitalAdminView.tsx`, including titles, counts, labels, and button text, all pertinent to the admin interface and queue management. Then I included the translation keys that were in the `GeminiLiveVoiceModal.tsx` file. Finally, I included the translation keys in the `SplitView.tsx` and `App.tsx` files.\n\n\n**Integrating Core Features**\n\nI am now focusing on fully integrating the AI health chat. I\'ve decided to make \"Chat\" a top-level tab in `MobileAppView.tsx` alongside the Home, SOS, Records, and Tokens tabs. This will enhance the user experience by making it an accessible core feature. I\'ll ensure it functions whether it is tapped on the main tab, or the home card. Additionally, I need to make sure the chat has multi-turn conversation support with memory and includes model selection with `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` and `gemini-3`. Also, I\'ve added a few localization keys to the translatable key list. They include `t.patientAppView`, `t.adminQueueView`, `t.monorepoView`, `t.liveVoiceBtn`, `t.aiChatBtn`, `t.servicesOperational`, and `t.medicalHubLocation`.\n\n\n"
