  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Requests**:\n  1. \"AI health chat is not integrated properly.\" Fix the AI health chat and deeply integrate it into the patient app workflow.\n  2. \"Also implement chat history.\" Provide persistent conversation history/sessions (save, list, resume, delete chat sessions backed by Firestore `/chat_conversations`).\n  3. \"Total Application language has to be changed when user changer his language.\" Implement comprehensive, seamless internationalization across Telugu (`te`), Hindi (`hi`), and English (`en`) across every screen and component.\n- **Scope & Constraints**:\n  - Zero hardcoded English strings on user-facing UI when Telugu or Hindi is selected.\n  - Multi-turn Gemini chat supporting `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, and `gemini-4-argon`.\n  - Injected `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` handling on the server, with fallback clinical knowledge engine in Telugu, Hindi, and English.\n  - Dev server running on port 3000 (`tsx server.ts`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed Components & Code Changes**:\n  1. `src/main.tsx`: Wrapped `<App />` in `<LanguageProvider>`.\n  2. `src/context/LanguageContext.tsx`: Full React Context storing active language (`te` by default), providing `setLanguage`, `t` dictionary, and syncing with `localStorage` and `api.updateProfile`.\n  3. `src/utils/translations.ts`: Complete translation dictionaries for `te`, `hi`, and `en` covering headers, navigation, voice triage, smart Rx decoder, SOS emergency, OPD tokens, health records, profile, hospital admin command center, live voice, and chatbot.\n  4. `src/App.tsx`:\n     - Global language selector added in the top header bar with one-click toggles (`\340\260\244\340\261\206\340\260\262\340\261\201\340\260\227\340\261\201`, `\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\202\340\244\246\340\245\200`, `English`).\n     - Translated all navigation tabs, titles, status badges, and footer via `t.*`.\n  5. `src/components/mobile/MobileAppView.tsx`:\n     - Added dedicated first-class `Chat` tab in the mobile bottom navigation bar (`Home`, `Chat`, `SOS`, `Records`, `Tokens`).\n     - Embedded in-app native chat screen with session dropdown selector, \"+ New Chat\", model switcher, quick prompt chips, and one-tap `\"Get OPD Token for this\"` button.\n     - Fully translated all greeting, hero cards, Rx scanner, live voice, tokens, emergency 108 helpline, and profile sections.\n  6. `src/components/chat/GeminiChatbotModal.tsx`:\n     - Desktop/modal chat with history drawer, Firestore sync (`chatStorage.ts`), copy button, model selector (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `gemini-4-argon`), roles, and quick prompt chips.\n  7. `src/components/mobile/DailyHealthInsightCard.tsx`: Translated metrics, labels, simulated badge, and weather/health observation tip via `t.*`.\n  8. `src/components/mobile/VoiceTriageSheet.tsx`: Translated recording states, tier banners (1/2/3), severity scores, digital tokens, patient instructions, clinical doctor summaries, and quick test presets.\n  9. `src/components/mobile/PrescriptionScannerSheet.tsx`: Translated photo capture/upload, strict clinical safety guardrail warning (`Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.`), and extracted dosages.\n  10. `src/components/mobile/SOSEmergencyButton.tsx`: Translated hold button, percentage ring, Priority 0 activation overlay, siren, ambient audio, and GPS dispatch stages.\n  11. `src/components/mobile/OPDTokensList.tsx`: Translated empty states, status badges, straight-line distance, and estimated wait times.\n  12. `src/components/mobile/HealthRecordsView.tsx`: Translated sub-tabs (Triage, Prescriptions, SOS logs) and empty state messages.\n  13. `src/components/admin/HospitalAdminView.tsx`: Translated hospital command center, live queue badge, metrics cards, priority ranking headers, department filter, and patient callback controls.\n  14. `src/components/live/GeminiLiveVoiceModal.tsx`: Translated live audio status, visualizer text, connection notices, and quick queries.\n  15. `src/components/SplitView.tsx`: Translated interactive dual-screen simulation mode banner.\n  16. `package.json`: Upgraded `@google/genai` to `^2.25.0` per skill guidelines for `gemini-3.8-*` and `gemini-4-argon`.\n  17. `src/server/gemini.ts` & `src/server/routes.ts`:\n     - Enhanced `/api/v1/chat` to accept `language` and pass language-specific system instructions.\n     - Added robust multilingual fallback clinical knowledge engine returning fluent, structured advice in Telugu script, Devanagari Hindi, or English.\n- **Verification Outcomes**:\n  - `compile_applet`: Build succeeded cleanly.\n  - `lint_applet`: Passed with zero TypeScript lint errors.\n  - `curl /api/health`: Exited with code 0, status \"healthy\".\n  - `curl /api/v1/chat` (Telugu): Successfully returned natural Telugu health advice.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- When running in an environment where `GEMINI_API_KEY` is not present, `chatWithGemini` must never return a plain generic English sentence when the user is speaking Telugu or Hindi. The fallback clinical engine now handles Telugu (`te`), Hindi (`hi`), and English (`en`) with medically appropriate instructions for fever, stomach pain, medicine dosages, and emergencies.\n- Adding `Chat` directly as a native tab inside the mobile frame drastically improves user experience and makes the AI health chat feel integral to the native mobile app rather than an auxiliary pop-up.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. *Chat English Fallback on Hindi/Telugu query*:\n   - Root Cause: In preview without an API key, `chatWithGemini` fell back to a hardcoded English string: `\"Sanjeevani Assistant (${modelChoice}): Thank you for reaching out...\"`.\n   - Fix: Added a multilingual clinical response rule engine in `src/server/gemini.ts` detecting Telugu, Hindi, or English and returning structured medical guidance in the matching script.\n2. *Old `@google/genai` version*:\n   - Root Cause: `package.json` had `@google/genai: ^2.4.0` while the `gemini-api` skill specifies `>= 2.25.0` for `gemini-3.8-*` and `gemini-4-argon`.\n   - Fix: Ran `install_applet_package` with `@google/genai@^2.25.0` and restarted the dev server.\n3. *Language toggle did not affect full application*:\n   - Root Cause: `LanguageProvider` was not mounted at the root (`src/main.tsx`), and individual subcomponents had hardcoded English strings.\n   - Fix: Mounted `LanguageProvider` around `<App />`, added synchronized language switchers in both the top navigation header and mobile status bar, and wired `useLanguage()` into all components.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (`tsx server.ts`).\n- Firestore is provisioned (`ai-studio-sanjeevanitriage-a37f31bb-2221-43e0-a139-6c5f97afa330`) and security rules are deployed.\n- Build and lint are completely clean (`tsc --noEmit` exits with 0).\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. In `src/server/routes.ts`, pass `language` in `chatWithGemini(messages, model, systemInstruction, language)` (currently `routes.ts` calls `chatWithGemini(messages, model, systemInstruction)` with 3 args). Update it to pass `language` as the 4th argument so the fallback engine explicitly uses the requested language.\n2. Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together to verify the 4th argument addition.\n3. Test a quick curl with `language: \"hi\"` to verify that Hindi responses are returned by `/api/v1/chat`.\n4. Present the final confirmation to the user.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Prescription safety protocol is absolute: illegible handwriting must return `\"Medicine name is unclear. Please consult a physical pharmacist.\"`\n- The Live Voice API must use `gemini-3.8-live`.\n- No pill-style buttons (adhere to `frontend-design` zero-pill discipline).\n- Maintain `metadata.json` with `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 221
    included_step_index_end: 343
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
